WEBVTT

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.530
Now's my chance!

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.110
Sohoku High School passed him!

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:23.000
There's 400 meters left!

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:26.170
<i>Now's my chance.</i>

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:30.920
<i>I passed Manami with 400 meters left.</i>

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:33.050
<i>Why did he slow down?</i>

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:34.670
<i>No, it doesn't matter.</i>

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:35.900
<i>I should be looking forward now.</i>

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:36.720
<i>It's in front of me...</i>

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.480
<i>It's right in front of me!</i>

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.430
<i>I see the red roof of the 
Akechidaira restaurant.</i>

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:44.440
<i>That's where the mountain result line is.</i>

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.080
<i>I'm almost there.</i>

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.690
<i>All my hairs are standing on end.</i>

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:51.150
<i>I have goosebumps.</i>

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:54.750
<i>Right now, I'm closest to the mountain line.</i>

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.660
<i>I'm about to get there first.</i>

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.030
<i>I've always dreamed of being first.</i>

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:05.620
<i>Is this what being first feels like?</i>

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:09.840
<i>I climbed so far. I pushed myself so hard.</i>

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.880
<i>But my legs feel unbelievably light.</i>

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:17.810
<i>I'll probably never forget this sight.</i>

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:21.390
Go, Sohoku High School! Keep going!

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:22.690
Take the mountains, #5!

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:24.140
Teshima, last spurt!

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:25.700
<i>I know.</i>

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.020
Go!

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:31.580
<i>Aoyagi, you'll probably be 
surprised by the results.</i>

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:34.030
<i>Here I go, Aoyagi.</i>

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:35.730
Don't worry about him! Just go!

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:37.110
Don't turn around!

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:40.180
<i>Don't worry? Don't turn around?</i>

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:41.870
<i>Keep going?</i>

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:08.350
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:23.240
<i>RIDE. 25 Look Up At The Sky</i>

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:20.530
Manami got off his bike?

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:21.720
What happened?

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.020
Are you okay? I'll hold your bike.

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:26.220
It's his chain. His chain came loose.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:29.680
What happens if your chain 
comes off during a race?

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:30.680
There's nothing you can do.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:34.930
The support car can bring you a 
spare wheel if you get a flat.

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:38.290
But you have to fix your chain on your own.

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:39.110
But...

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:43.170
An experienced rider should be able to 
return to the race in less than a minute.

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:47.390
But sometimes that can decide the race.

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:50.860
It can be caused by the smallest thing,
and it's terrible luck.

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:54.880
But I thought bicycle races 
were supposed to be fair.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:59.400
Sometimes riders do wait when their 
opponents have mechanical issues.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:00.770
If they notice, that is.

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:01.800
You mean...

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:08.180
If they don't notice or claim they didn't,
there's nothing anyone can say.

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:10.350
His chain's back on!

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:11.770
Go, Manami!

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:13.230
Don't give up!

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:14.500
Hakone Academy High School!

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:15.480
You can still make it!

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:19.450
<i>I can still make it?</i>

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:23.030
<i>I lost 15 to 20 seconds just now.</i>

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:27.910
<i>I can't make that up in 400 meters.</i>

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:30.250
Will Hakone Academy High 
School's rider catch up?

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:32.100
No, probably not.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.470
They're right before the finish line.

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:36.250
If I were Sohoku High School,
I wouldn't wait.

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:39.380
Go!

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:54.980
<i>H-He... stopped?</i>

00:04:56.600 --> 00:05:00.200
<i>Teshima-san waited for me?</i>

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.450
<i>He noticed what happened?</i>

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:05.770
<i>But there's 300 meters left.</i>

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:09.020
<i>He can see the mountain result line.</i>

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:13.370
<i>It's his chance to win the mountain tag 
for Sohoku High School.</i>

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:21.710
<i>No one would've blamed him for going.</i>

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:24.990
Teshima-san...

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:33.100
Why?

00:05:34.610 --> 00:05:38.100
I know it's stupid, too.

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:41.650
But the view was incredible.

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:43.730
So I was taking a tea break.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:52.740
I'll find another chance 
with my own strength!

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:55.250
I'll ride with everything I've got!

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.250
Bring in on, Manami!

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:00.740
Manami!

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:02.010
Teshima-san!

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:03.790
<i>Three hundred meters left!</i>

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:04.510
The final...

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:06.340
Battle!

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:08.100
Two hundred and fifty meters left!

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.260
So fast!

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:12.670
Go, Hakone Academy High School!

00:06:12.670 --> 00:06:14.430
Don't let him beat you, Sohoku High School!

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:16.430
<i>Fight, Junta!</i>

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:18.350
Go!

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:18.350
<i>All out!</i>

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:38.120
Neither one's giving any ground!

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:40.280
Manami-san, take it!

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:40.600
Hakone Academy High School!

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:42.380
Manami-san, fight!

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:42.380
Hakone Academy High School

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:43.490
Chiba, you got this!

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:44.940
Sohoku

00:06:43.490 --> 00:06:44.920
Teshima!

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:46.610
<i>I can't feel anything.</i>

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:49.430
<i>The tingling feeling is gone, too.</i>

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:56.470
<i>This is probably bad, but I'm 
moving toward my target.</i>

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:01.230
<i>Bring it on, body!
One hundred and fifty meters left!</i>

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:06.350
<i>Go! I believe!</i>

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:07.650
<i>I believe in miracles!</i>

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:09.670
They're passing through the 
disaster prevention tunnel!

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:11.910
There's 100 meters left to the finish line!

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:13.410
<i>All out...</i>

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:16.330
<i>All out, all out, all out.</i>

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:19.250
<i>Every moment is once in a lifetime.</i>

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:21.250
<i>There's only one chance to achieve results.</i>

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:22.740
<i>That's why I ride all out!</i>

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:24.310
Eighty meters left!

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:25.250
They're neck and neck!

00:07:25.690 --> 00:07:27.630
<i>Isn't that right, Toudou-san?</i>

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:31.300
What?

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:33.720
You're giving #3 to me?

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:37.980
That's right. It's the number of
Hakone Academy High School's mountain ace.

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:42.560
It's yours. Wear #3 at the next Inter-High.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:45.500
But there's Kuroda-san...

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:47.490
I've talked to him.

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:49.070
He said it's not a problem.

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:51.100
Is it heavy?

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:53.740
<i>#3...</i>

00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:58.410
I guess you'll be 13, though.

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:01.340
That's an unlucky number.

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:03.920
You could flip it upside down 
if you're superstitious.

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:09.050
I'll wear it right side up and overcome it.

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:11.530
That sounds like you.

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:14.180
<i>I'll overcome!</i>

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:15.400
<i>Manami!</i>

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:16.550
<i>Teshima-san!</i>

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:22.310
<i>Nothing's ever easy.</i>

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:25.770
<i>I wasn't expecting him to keep up with me.</i>

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:28.940
<i>I didn't think he'd wait for me 
when I had mechanical trouble.</i>

00:08:29.890 --> 00:08:31.410
<i>I thought it was over.</i>

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:33.690
<i>But I'm still riding.</i>

00:08:33.690 --> 00:08:37.200
<i>And it's hard. That's why...</i>

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:39.440
I'm going all out!

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:41.200
Grab your dream!

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:46.600
Now's my chance! My only chance!

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:49.000
I'll overcome!

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:50.880
Sixty meters left!

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:51.880
Fifty!

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:53.010
Forty!

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:53.880
Thirty!

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:55.080
This is it!

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:55.720
Who will it be?

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:57.220
Ten meters left!

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:58.110
<i>Get there...</i>

00:08:58.110 --> 00:08:58.860
<i>Get there...</i>

00:08:58.860 --> 00:08:59.680
<i>My wheels!</i>

00:09:04.130 --> 00:09:05.350
It's the announcement.

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:19.990
Two wishes...

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:23.580
But only one can come true.

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:26.770
A battle between climbers is brutal.

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:31.610
That's why the winner shines 
beyond the shadow of a doubt.

00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:40.100
<i>Hakone Academy High School's
Manami Sangaku has taken the mountains!</i>

00:09:47.090 --> 00:09:50.540
<i>The first day of the Inter-High 
and Irohazaka has been won</i>

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:51.730
<i>by Hakone Academy High School!</i>

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:54.570
<i>Number 13 is the new Mountain God!</i>

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:58.950
<i>Manami Sangaku! He's shouting!</i>

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:00.980
All right!

00:10:00.980 --> 00:10:02.250
Yeah!

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:04.350
Manami, good job!

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:05.370
Manami-san!

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:07.450
We're the strongest!

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:11.820
I've never seen Manami 
shout after he's won before.

00:10:15.890 --> 00:10:18.630
<i>I did it, Toudou-san.</i>

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:20.600
<i>I overcame it.</i>

00:10:30.110 --> 00:10:32.440
<i>I didn't make it.</i>

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:36.230
<i>I gave everything I had to be first.</i>

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:39.750
<i>We were tied just a few meters 
before the finish line.</i>

00:10:41.650 --> 00:10:44.120
<i>We were neck and neck, but he got past me.</i>

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:51.100
<i>When he'd already given everything 
he had, he still had more to give.</i>

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:55.200
<i>He's amazing. He must be a prodigy.</i>

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:56.920
<i>Manami's amazing.</i>

00:10:57.370 --> 00:11:02.680
<i>Hard work is useless 
against someone like him.</i>

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:05.060
Teshima-san...

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:13.770
Thank you.

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:17.610
For waiting.

00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:23.140
I told you.

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:26.740
I was just enjoying my tea time.

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:30.170
I didn't wait for you.

00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:32.710
You don't need to thank me.

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:35.420
I just...

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:40.170
I want everyone who takes cycling seriously...

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:44.430
to be equal while they're riding.

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:47.910
That thought made me hit the brakes.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:53.770
But holding onto ideals like equality 
are why everyone calls me ordinary.

00:11:54.590 --> 00:11:55.640
Teshima-san!

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:57.520
You were strong.

00:11:58.100 --> 00:12:03.070
You kept up with my attacks 
countless times at the Inter-High.

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:06.910
Normally, a person wouldn't 
wait at 300 meters.

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:11.080
They'd say it could be fixed quickly.
That it was bad luck.

00:12:11.390 --> 00:12:14.240
That I was just unlucky.

00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:16.050
Everyone wants to win.

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:18.550
The climber's medal was 
right in front of you.

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:20.650
But you stopped.

00:12:20.650 --> 00:12:24.350
A man who does things others can't is strong.

00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:31.390
Don't flatter me.

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:34.220
I'm weak.

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:39.520
Teshima was a close second?

00:12:39.870 --> 00:12:40.610
Is it true?

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:43.030
Yes, he was milliseconds behind.

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:47.610
Isn't this amazing?

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:50.990
See? I told you he could do it.

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:52.540
Second blows, though.

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:54.920
<i>Teshima, you...</i>

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:55.920
Wow.

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:58.020
What happened?

00:12:58.020 --> 00:13:00.810
The report doesn't say exactly.

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:03.940
But it says #13 had mechanical problems.

00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:04.950
Manami did?

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:07.470
Is that when he caught up?

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:09.510
Had he fallen behind?

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:12.980
I don't think so, Danchiku.

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:13.640
What?

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:17.100
I don't know how the mechanical 
issues affected the race,

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:24.360
but I think Teshima-san worked hard 
to stick to Manami the whole time.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:33.950
<b>Mountain Results</b>

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:33.950
<b>Manami Sangaku</b>

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:33.950
<b>Kanagawa
Hakone Academy
 High School</b>

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:33.950
<b>Teshima Junta</b>

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:33.950
<b>Chiba
Sohoku
 High School</b>

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:40.960
That was really close, though.

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:43.050
He's the man who makes it happen.

00:13:43.660 --> 00:13:45.340
Well done, Manami.

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:48.800
No, perhaps I should be
praising the other man instead.

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:53.890
I'm impressed Teshima-kun was able 
to keep up with his ordinary riding.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:56.880
Manami seems to have enjoyed himself.

00:13:56.880 --> 00:13:59.100
But that doesn't change the results.

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:01.110
Too bad, Sohoku High School.

00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:04.110
Your leader lost.

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:05.700
<i>Teshima-san...</i>

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:06.940
<i>Teshima-san...</i>

00:14:06.940 --> 00:14:07.820
<i>Teshima-san...</i>

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:10.320
Teshima-san is amazing!

00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:12.530
<i>Junta, you're...</i>

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:15.790
That's amazing. Honestly, I'm on fire now.

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:17.270
I'm trembling with excitement.

00:14:17.270 --> 00:14:19.920
Teshima-san, I'm sorry for making fun of you.

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:25.650
I wish I could go right now 
and race to the finish line.

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:27.220
You'd better not.

00:14:28.940 --> 00:14:31.070
So the permed one did it.

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:32.640
Our leader is...

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:36.310
Yeah. A hard worker who 
does what he says he'll do.

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:38.730
He's Teshima Junta.

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:45.170
Watch out!

00:14:45.170 --> 00:14:46.990
#5 is falling!

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:46.990
Teshima-san?

00:14:49.970 --> 00:14:51.620
<i>I can finally lie down.</i>

00:14:52.510 --> 00:14:54.510
<i>I seriously gave everything.</i>

00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:58.910
<i>I probably won't be able to 
get up again if I lie down now.</i>

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:03.180
<i>Sorry, Imaizumi and Naruko.</i>

00:15:04.010 --> 00:15:07.130
<i>The rest is up to you, Aoyagi.</i>

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:09.990
<i>Dropping out after the first day...</i>

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:12.570
<i>I really am weak.</i>

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:14.560
<i>I've failed as their captain.</i>

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:18.610
<i>But sorry, I can't move anymore.</i>

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:21.750
<i>It'll be just the five of you.</i>

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:25.070
<i>Sorry, Sohoku High School.</i>

00:15:27.810 --> 00:15:29.370
Teshima-san!

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:30.360
It's another Sohoku rider!

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:35.530
Gotta make it!

00:15:47.870 --> 00:15:50.590
It's you, Onoda.

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:52.450
I made it.

00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:53.370
It's #1!

00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:56.210
I pedaled as hard as I could when I saw you.

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:55.750
Sohoku High School's #1 came!

00:15:56.590 --> 00:15:58.100
I'm glad I made it.

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:02.940
What are you doing here?

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:06.180
I got your message.

00:16:06.180 --> 00:16:11.900
Imaizumi-kun gave me permission 
to come support you.

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:16.200
And...

00:16:18.230 --> 00:16:19.330
To give you these water bottles.

00:16:21.150 --> 00:16:23.120
They thought you'd be parched.

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:25.330
They're from Imaizumi-kun and Naruko-kun.

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:28.030
<i>I'm standing.</i>

00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:33.130
<i>Does that mean I can keep going?</i>

00:16:33.650 --> 00:16:35.340
<i>A team that supports each other...</i>

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:39.910
<i>Yes, that's the kind of team 
Sohoku High School is.</i>

00:16:40.740 --> 00:16:42.130
Support, huh?

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:50.440
Thanks for the help, Onoda.

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:57.530
Let's ride a little longer.

00:16:57.530 --> 00:16:58.350
Yes, sir.

00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:12.680
Hakone Academy High School 
took the mountains.

00:17:12.680 --> 00:17:15.380
Sohoku High School came in second and third.

00:17:16.120 --> 00:17:20.470
<i>So you caught up, Sakamichi.</i>

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:23.750
The guys in front of us are 
probably increasing their pace.

00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:30.740
In that case, shall we 
go as well, Komari-kun?

00:17:30.740 --> 00:17:31.560
Yes.

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:35.490
Hakone Academy High School 
just took the mountains.

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:37.950
Hakone Academy High School's so strong.

00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:43.790
It's Hakone Academy High School!

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:45.330
They've increased their pace!

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:47.250
Sohoku High School's keeping up!

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:52.590
Doubashi took the flats. 
Manami took the mountains.

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:54.800
All that's left is the finish line.

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:01.070
Should we go a little faster?

00:18:01.070 --> 00:18:02.850
Not too fast, Yuto.

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:06.550
All we have to do now is strike fear 
in the hearts of Sohoku High School.

00:18:06.550 --> 00:18:09.400
There's still more than ten 
kilometers to the finish line.

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:12.650
Roger that.

00:18:14.620 --> 00:18:18.040
<i>I see. They're fast, but...</i>

00:18:18.610 --> 00:18:20.200
Not too fast.

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:22.280
Just so-so.

00:18:22.750 --> 00:18:27.520
They're trying to pull ahead 
of us, but they can't.

00:18:27.520 --> 00:18:28.460
Yeah.

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:33.520
Onoda overcame a hopeless time 
difference and caught up to the front.

00:18:33.520 --> 00:18:34.750
And most importantly...

00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:38.720
He received Teshima-san's 
passionate vibrations.

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:40.760
We never give up.

00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:43.880
Let's go, Sohoku High School!

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:44.760
Yeah!

00:18:52.680 --> 00:18:54.270
The first day of the Inter-High...

00:18:55.220 --> 00:18:57.670
The final battle is about to begin.

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:52.950
Dear brother

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:56.460
Dear brother

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:02.070
Dear brother

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:07.660
Sorry, Bro.

00:21:09.190 --> 00:21:15.420
Anyway, they've got directions, announcements,
automatic doors, and moving sidewalks.

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:16.670
They've even got AC.

00:21:17.100 --> 00:21:18.810
They're too considerate.

00:21:24.370 --> 00:21:26.090
So hot.

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:28.700
It's so humid.

00:21:28.700 --> 00:21:31.370
It feels like summer in Japan.

00:21:31.370 --> 00:21:32.430
Nothing's like it.

00:21:33.170 --> 00:21:36.980
I really feel like I'm back in Japan.

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:44.070
Nah, it's too hot.

00:21:44.550 --> 00:21:48.030
I'm amazed I rode in this heat last year.

00:21:48.830 --> 00:21:51.420
They're riding right now.

00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:57.250
I meant to arrive just before they 
started to inspire Sakamichi,

00:21:57.580 --> 00:22:00.890
but my flight was six hours late.

00:22:00.890 --> 00:22:03.100
We waited a long time for you.

00:22:03.100 --> 00:22:03.670
What?

00:22:08.110 --> 00:22:10.360
Makishima, how have you been?

00:22:10.360 --> 00:22:12.100
K-Kinjou!

00:22:13.570 --> 00:22:15.180
<i>Calm down, Yusuke.</i>

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:18.150
<i>Kinjou couldn't possibly be here.</i>

00:22:18.150 --> 00:22:20.050
<i>I'm just hallucinating 
because of the jet lag.</i>

00:22:20.050 --> 00:22:21.770
How's life in England?

00:22:21.770 --> 00:22:22.460
Huh?

00:22:23.460 --> 00:22:24.960
It's been a while.

00:22:24.960 --> 00:22:26.070
<i>It's really him.</i>

00:22:26.900 --> 00:22:28.030
Kinjou!

00:22:28.030 --> 00:22:29.110
Makishima.

00:22:29.110 --> 00:22:31.770
What are you doing here?

00:22:31.770 --> 00:22:35.670
When I called your house,
they told me you were coming back.

00:22:35.670 --> 00:22:37.330
You're going to the Inter-High, right?

00:22:37.330 --> 00:22:38.180
Huh?

00:22:38.790 --> 00:22:41.730
Let's hurry. The race has already started.

00:22:41.730 --> 00:22:44.110
You've been waiting for six hours.

00:22:44.110 --> 00:22:46.250
You could've gone without me.

00:22:46.250 --> 00:22:51.590
Someone said we have to 
wait for anyone who's late.

00:22:54.120 --> 00:22:57.350
Hey. How long were you going 
to make us wait, Makishima?

00:22:57.350 --> 00:22:59.570
T-Tadokorocchi...

00:22:59.570 --> 00:23:01.730
We can talk later. Get in.

00:23:01.730 --> 00:23:02.440
Sure.

00:23:06.470 --> 00:23:07.860
Will we make it in time for the race?

00:23:07.860 --> 00:23:09.070
Who do you think you're talking to?

00:23:09.450 --> 00:23:13.870
I'm Sohoku High School's human 
bullet train, Tadokoro Jin.

00:23:19.410 --> 00:23:22.460
Oxygen!

00:23:25.020 --> 00:23:30.010
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles* on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.

00:23:26.070 --> 00:23:30.010
*and cars
